### SBD403 A3 manual demo (VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client)
### Setup: run the API (`dotnet run --project SBD.API --launch-profile https`), then put the values below in your
### REST Client environment or replace them by hand. Nothing real is stored in this file: passwords come from your .env.
### Note: the API accepts TLS 1.3 only; clients built on macOS .NET/Secure Transport may not connect (see evidence/tls-check.txt).
### Calls must come from an address in Security__AllowedIps; /admin calls from Security__AdminAllowedIps.

@host = https://localhost:7044
@apiKey = {{$dotenv Security__ApiKey}}
@normalUser = normal.user
@normalPassword = {{$dotenv SEED_NORMAL_PASSWORD}}
@accountingUser = accounting.user
@accountingPassword = {{$dotenv SEED_ACCOUNTING_PASSWORD}}
@privilegedUser = privileged.user
@privilegedPassword = {{$dotenv SEED_PRIVILEGED_PASSWORD}}
@adminUser = user.admin
@adminPassword = {{$dotenv SEED_USERADMIN_PASSWORD}}

### 1. Normal user logs in (password only, no MFA)  [A8]
# @name normalLogin
POST {{host}}/auth/login
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{normalUser}}", "password": "{{normalPassword}}" }

###
@normalToken = {{normalLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 2. Accounting login step 1: the reply asks for MFA and returns a ticket  [A8]
# @name accountingLogin
POST {{host}}/auth/login
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{accountingUser}}", "password": "{{accountingPassword}}" }

### 2b. First login only: GET the authenticator key with /auth/mfa/setup, add it to an authenticator app, then confirm with /auth/mfa/confirm
POST {{host}}/auth/mfa/setup
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mfaTicket": "{{accountingLogin.response.body.$.mfaTicket}}" }

### 2c. Step 2: send the 6-digit code from the authenticator app  (use /auth/mfa/confirm for the first enrolment)
# @name accountingMfa
POST {{host}}/auth/mfa
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mfaTicket": "{{accountingLogin.response.body.$.mfaTicket}}", "code": "000000" }

###
@accountingToken = {{accountingMfa.response.body.$.token}}

### 3. Privileged login: repeat steps 2, 2b and 2c with privileged.user, then set @privilegedToken from the reply
@privilegedToken = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### 4. Search as Normal: name, address and phone only  [R1]
POST {{host}}/customers/search
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{normalToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lastName": "Smith*" }

### 5. Same search as Accounting: adds the masked card  [R1]
POST {{host}}/customers/search
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accountingToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lastName": "Smith*" }

### 6. Same search as Privileged: adds the medical status  [R1]
POST {{host}}/customers/search
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{privilegedToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lastName": "Smith*" }

### 7. Injection attempt: refused with 400, never run as SQL  [V1]
POST {{host}}/customers/search
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{normalToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lastName": "' OR '1'='1" }

### 8. Normal cannot reveal a card: 403  [R5]
POST {{host}}/customers/1/card/reveal
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{normalToken}}

### 9. Accounting reveals a card: allowed and written to AuditLog  [R5]
POST {{host}}/customers/1/card/reveal
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accountingToken}}

### 10. Wrong key: 401 before anything else runs  [E6]
POST {{host}}/customers/search
X-Api-Key: wrong
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lastName": "Smith" }

### 11. User Admin (from the internal address) signs in with MFA, then manages accounts.  [R6]
### Repeat steps 2, 2b and 2c with user.admin and set @adminToken.
@adminToken = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### 11a. A User Admin cannot search customer data: 403  [R6]
POST {{host}}/customers/search
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lastName": "Smith" }

### 11b. Create a user (approval reference required)  [R6]
POST {{host}}/admin/users
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "demo.person", "role": "Normal", "temporaryPassword": "REPLACE-WITH-A-15-CHAR-TEMP-PASSWORD", "approvalRef": "CHG-1001" }

### 11c. Change a role without an approval reference: 400  [R6]
POST {{host}}/admin/users/USER_ID/role
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "Accounting" }

### 11d. Change a role with one: sessions of that user end at once  [R6]
POST {{host}}/admin/users/USER_ID/role
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "Accounting", "approvalRef": "CHG-1002" }

### 11e. Disable, password reset, MFA reset and search unlock follow the same pattern
POST {{host}}/admin/users/USER_ID/disable
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "approvalRef": "CHG-1003" }

### 12. Lockout: five wrong passwords, then the sixth login is refused even with the right one  [A6]
POST {{host}}/auth/login
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{normalUser}}", "password": "wrong-password-0000" }

### 13. Logout ends the session: the token stops working  [A10]
POST {{host}}/auth/logout
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{normalToken}}
